# Copy to .env (gitignored). Everything has a working default.
#
# THIS FILE IS READ ON RANK 0 ONLY. Both ranks are launched from up.sh on this
# node, so there is no second .env to keep in step - that is the point.

# HF_TOKEN=hf_...

# The two numbers that trade against each other. ~22 GiB of KV per node buys
# either context or concurrency, not both. Raising MAX_NUM_SEQS without
# lowering MAX_MODEL_LEN is how you get preemption instead of throughput.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=131072
# MAX_NUM_SEQS=6
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE 1M-CONTEXT PATH, and what it costs
#
# 1M context on two GB10s is real, but it needs `nvfp4_ds_mla` - a sparse-MLA
# KV dtype with a 584-byte envelope per token. Upstream vLLM does not have it;
# it comes from the DSpark fork lineage, which also carries a stack of
# DeepSeek-specific hotfixes and is reported by its own authors to beat newer
# upstream by 8-9% on decode.
#
# Taking it means pinning this model to one fork's release cadence. That is a
# real trade, not a free upgrade - see docs/decisions.md#two-node-vllm for why
# this repo declines forks by default.
#
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/anemll/dspark-vllm-gx10:0.1.1
# KV_CACHE_DTYPE=nvfp4_ds_mla
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=1048576
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.835
#
# The fork also wants these, and they are inert on upstream:
#   VLLM_USE_BREAKABLE_CUDAGRAPH=0     reported mandatory for its performance
#   VLLM_USE_B12X_WO_PROJECTION=1      Stage-C NVFP4 runtime
# Pass them through with EXTRA_ENV, which up.sh hands to both ranks:
# EXTRA_ENV=(-e VLLM_USE_BREAKABLE_CUDAGRAPH=0 -e VLLM_USE_B12X_WO_PROJECTION=1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Speculative decoding. 5 draft tokens; the model card says 7, but it is
# written for a 4xGB300 node where a rejected draft costs less.
# SPEC_CONFIG={"method":"dspark","num_speculative_tokens":5,"draft_sample_method":"greedy"}
#
# NEVER OMIT num_speculative_tokens on the fork image above. On that lineage
# the DSpark branch that would derive it is absent, so the value falls back to
# num_nextn_predict_layers = 1: the server boots, speculates one token per
# step, and reports nothing unusual. You lose most of the speed the fork was
# taken for, silently. `ws up vllm-bench-serve` shows the tok/step that gives
# it away.
#
# To turn it off entirely and measure the difference:
# SPEC_CONFIG=null

# Rendezvous. Auto-detected from the default route.
# MASTER_ADDR=192.168.1.70
# PEER=poseidon

# Leave IB_HCA unset unless a log shows the wrong RDMA device chosen - measured
# here, NCCL discovers both ACTIVE ports and skips the two DOWN ones.
# IB_HCA=rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0

# 8890, so it does not collide with the other serving workspaces on 8888/8899.
# PORT=8890

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FP4 INDEXER CACHE, which is OFF here and is in every official launch line
# for this model. Not an oversight: on GB10 it crash-loops the worker at init
#
#   ValueError: indexer_kv_dtype='mxfp4' requires Blackwell datacenter GPUs
#   (sm_10x, e.g. B200/GB200); sm_120 (consumer Blackwell) and earlier
#   architectures are not supported.
#
# because the recipes it comes from run on GB200/B200 and this box is sm_121.
# Set it on a datacenter Blackwell node, where it is a real win:
# ATTENTION_CONFIG={"use_fp4_indexer_cache": true}
